Gimmix
======

Gimmix is a graphical client for the Music Player Daemon (MPD), written in
C with GTK 3.

Features
--------
* Simple and clean interface, with a compact mode that shows only the
  player controls.
* Library browser and library search (by artist, album, title or file name).
* Playlist management (load, save and delete MPD playlists).
* Album covers, from image files next to the music or from the Cover Art
  Archive (https://coverartarchive.org).
* Lyrics from LRCLIB (https://lrclib.net).
* Tag editing with TagLib.
* System tray icon with a notification tooltip, volume control by mouse
  wheel and a playback menu.
* Keyboard control.

Requirements
------------
* GTK >= 3.22
* GLib >= 2.32
* libmpd >= 0.17.0
* TagLib >= 1.4 (C bindings), for the tag editor; disable with
  --disable-tageditor
* libcurl >= 7.19.4 and json-glib >= 1.2, for the cover and lyrics
  plugins; disable with --disable-cover and --disable-lyrics

Gimmix works with MPD 0.16 or later.

Installation
------------
From a release tarball:

    ./configure
    make
    make install

From a git checkout, run ./autogen.sh first. It needs autoconf, automake,
gettext (autopoint) and pkg-config. See INSTALL for details.

Configuration
-------------
Gimmix is configured from its preferences dialog. The settings are stored
in ~/.gimmixrc; the first start shows a dialog that asks for the MPD
connection. The valid settings are listed in the gimmix(1) manual page.

Set music_directory to the directory MPD plays from. The tag editor needs
it to find the files, and the cover plugin looks there for cover.jpg,
folder.jpg and similar images next to the music.

Covers and lyrics that were fetched are kept in ~/.gimmix/covers and
~/.gimmix/lyrics. Right-click the cover to set one from a file or to
fetch it again.

Keybindings
-----------
    z        Previous song
    x, c     Play / pause
    v        Stop
    b        Next song
    i        Song information and tag editor
    r        Toggle repeat
    s        Toggle shuffle
    l        Show or hide the playlist

The mouse wheel on the system tray icon or the volume button changes the
volume.

Bugs
----
Please report bugs at https://github.com/nyxdis/gimmix/issues with a
description, the steps to reproduce them and the versions of gimmix,
GTK, libmpd and MPD.

Authors
-------
Gimmix was written by Priyank M. Gosalia and is maintained by Freydis
Mende. See AUTHORS for everyone who contributed.
